1 NOTE <p>Isabella sailed with her sister, Mary A.,on Sept. 21, 1912 from Glasgow on the Scandinavian and arrived at Quebec on Sept. 29.  They then travelled by train (CPR) to Toronto.  She was 25 and Mary A
2 CONC nne was 18.  John Liney sailed on the Grampian which left Glasgow on July 6, 1912 and arrived in Quebec on July 14.  He also took the train to Toronto.  It looks like his age was 23.  His fellow trave
2 CONC llers were:  Michael Joseph Dillon and Patrick Dillon.</p>
1 NOTE Both Isabella and John came to Canada in 1912 and then the story goes that they went to the US for a short time and then back to Canada.
