1 IMMI Bridget Driscoll Passenger Record  Bridget Driscoll was 18 years old when she arrived in New York City. She departed Cobh on 29 Aug 1926 on the S.S. Cedric and arrived at the port of New York on 6 Sep 1926. Her closest relative was listed as Father, Mr Michael Driscoll, Reen, Ballinskelly’s [record spelling], Caherciveen, Co. Kerry.  Bridget was bound for New York. Her sister Miss Driscoll at 38 West 10th Street New York paid for her passage, and Bridget was headed to her friend Mr James O’Shea 518 West 132 Street New York City, N.Y. Her complexion was fresh and the color of her eyes and hair were brown according to the passenger record.
