2 CONC ve during the 30s and 40s.</p> <p>He was employed as a plastering sub-contractor on the new Creggan Estate in 1947-50, then on the Coach Road housing development (this became an extension of the Lone 
2 CONC Moor Road to it's junction with the Letterkenny Road) &nbsp;He set up business as a building contractor after this and built houses, worked on local housing schemes etc until the early 60s when his bu
