1 NOTE Born Mary Elizabeth "Lillian" Kellagher in Saint Clair, PA, she graduated from Saint Clair High School as class valedictorian in 1945. After graduation, she attended Ford Business School and worked as
2 CONC  a bookkeeper for radio station WPPA in Pottsville, PA.  In March 1951, she married Walter Joseph Sincoskie of Mill Creek. After living briefly in Baltimore, MD and Louisville, KY, they settled in Wil
2 CONC mington, DE. In 1971, she graduated summa cum laude, Phi Beta Kappa and first in her class in English from the University of Delaware. She then taught English for several years at Delcastle Technical 
2 CONC High School and Goldey-Beacom College, while continuing graduate studies. She was widowed in 1972.  In 1978, she married Harold D. Sheaffer and moved to Harrisburg, PA. A homemaker for the rest of her
2 CONC  life, Mrs. Sheaffer also taught English to adult students as a volunteer. She was married for 22 years until Mr. Sheaffer's death in 2000.  Mrs. Sheaffer was the daughter of Anna Fedorisko Kellagher 
2 CONC and James V. Kellagher, both deceased. She was survived by a son, Walter David Sincoskie of Hampton, NJ; a daughter, Laura Sincoskie Kurmas of Ocean City, NJ; a sister, Jean Connors of Saint Clair, PA
2 CONC  and two granddaughters, Jamie and Anna Kurmas of Ocean City, NJ.   =Sources=  https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~cullather/genealogy/FAMTREE/index.htm?ssmain=e2094.htm;  https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~
2 CONC cullather/genealogy/FAMTREE/index.htm?ssmain=p5491.htm;  https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/107208170/mary-lillian-sincoskie  https://www.ancestry.co.uk/search/collections/1030/?name=_Sincoskie
