1 NOTE !death was an aproximation from lease transferes in local newspappers;lived and married near Carrigart;  Michael:  See Below: James Logue Married a Bridget Coyle.  Owen B.1888 You speak of was my gran
2 CONC dfather.  His actual birth was 23 Feb 1888 but and was baptized a few days later. His parents did not register it for a few months and Owen thought it funny to put one over on the British.  Here is th
2 CONC e family:  James Logue b. 1834 d. 1930 (owen's Father) Married first Bridget Coyle b 1847 d. 1880 or so. Offspring: Patrick Logue B. 1872 He was a boat pilot John b. 1874 Pilot Instructor for the Iris
2 CONC h Government Anne B. 1876 Married Dennis McBride Daniel b. 1878 He went to the US and then went back to Ireland  Married Secondly Sarah McBride b 1858 d. 1890 Offspring Hugh Logue 1882 Went to Austral
2 CONC ia and died there James b. 1884 Went to the US and went back to inherit wife's father's farm Michael b. 1886 He was an Ill and was in the same crib he was born in at age 21 when he died. Owen b. 1888 
2 CONC My grandfather was a shoemaker and lived in Philly Peter b. 1889 Was a Merchant Marrine and went to australia died at age of 102 Mary b. 1890 Died just after birth along with mother.  James Logue B 18
2 CONC 34 Father was: Patrick Logue b. 1796 His Father was: James Logue b. 1754 His Father was: Owen O'Logue b. 1720 His Father was: O'Logue b. 1695 on the Inch Island, Donegal, Ireland  I have been over in 
2 CONC Ireland about 9 times doing research and have been under the benifit of a book on the Logues going back about 400 years. O'Logue told his children that they were to memorize their ancestors going back
2 CONC  to 1550's but that memory did not survive. Neither did the book, although everyone has seen it, it was misplaced? in Australia in about 1965 or so.  Joe Reiley
