4 CONC lle, a daughter of the late John and Elizabeth, nee Stahl, Reichwein. She lived in the community until eight years ago when she came to Ashland to make her home with the Millers. She was a member of S
4 CONC t. Mauritius Church of Ashland, the Rosary Society, and the Catholic Daughters of America. Her husband, the late August Klusman, died sixteen years ago and surviving are these children: Edward and Fra
4 CONC nk of Lavelle; Joseph of Brady, Christine, wife of Bernard Miller, with whom she resided, and Margaret, wife of Michael Klusman of Philadelphia. Surviving brothers and sisters are Mrs. Elizabeth Scheu
4 CONC ren and Peter Reichwein of Lavelle, John and Christine Reichwein of Locust Gap, and Frank Reichwein of Shamokin. Seventeen grandchildren also survive. The funeral will be held Saturday morning from th
4 CONC e Miller home with Solemn High Mass in St. Mauritius Church at 10 o&#039;clock and interment in the parish cemetery. Relatives and friends are invite to attend the funeral. Frank L Burke is the funera
4 CONC l director.
