4 CONC  55, sec. 6, row 16 adj. names Staudenmeier, Ferner (names are at top of cem) === Rec&#039;d 12/3/2015: ASHLAND DAILY NEWS-Friday, December 26, 1930 Jos. Reichwein Dies Suddenly At Lavelle Joseph Reic
4 CONC hwein, about 36, one of the best known men of this section and for years a dairyman, is dead today at his home in Lavelle. This morning today at 1:10 o&#039;clock he was seized with an attack of acute
4 CONC  indigestion and twenty minutes later the end came. He was still apparently in good health yesterday and the shock of the Christmas tragedy affected not only his family but those who knew this young m
4 CONC an. Born and raised in Lavelle Mr. Reichwein spent all his life in that town working about the Reichwein Dairy operated by his father John Reichwein, and later his sons, for the past 35 years. Joseph 
4 CONC was a member of St. Mauritius church and the St. Mauritius Society. He was a member of the Ashland Elks, Moose and Eagles and of the Lavelle lodge of Red Men. He took an active roll in the Elk&#039;s 
4 CONC Bowling League and was a member of Dr. Frank Grady&#039;s team. He was a man of fine character and held the highest esteem of all who knew him. The oldest of three brothers in active charge of Reichwe
4 CONC in Dairy he was looked upon as the one in charge at all times. He is survived by his widow and two children, Anna and Joseph Jr. His 80 year old father John Reichwein and the following brothers and si
4 CONC sters also survive: Peter, of Lavelle, John, of Locust Gap, Frank, of Norristown, Mrs. Clem Scheuren, of Lavelle, Mrs.August Vogel, of Norristown, Mrs. August Kluseman, of Lavelle, Christiana, of Lave
4 CONC lle, and Mrs. John Quirk, of Lavelle. The funeral will be held Monday morning with mass in St. Mauritius church at Ashland at 9:30 o&#039;clock after which interment will be made in the parish cemeter
4 CONC y with Director Higgins of Mt. Carmel in charge. Friends and relatives are invited to attend the funeral.
