1 NOTE <p>Anthony left school at 14 and attended Hughes' academy at night. </p><p><p>He joined the GPO aged 14 as a message boy and worked his way up unitl he was senior overseer.  When he retired aged 60 he
2 CONC  received a medal and certificate for 45 years of faithful service.</p></p><p><p>During WWI he was a morse-code operator at Burtonport.</p></p><p><p>He was very musical; he trained and conducted choir
2 CONC s and won lots of prizes.  At the Feis Ceol in Dublin he was beaten by John Mc Cormack by just one point.</p></p><p><p>His poetry was originally published in the Derry Journal.</p></p><p><p>He wrote a
2 CONC  weekly column for the "Journal" about obscure Irish saints under the pen-name Veritas</p></p><p><p> (c) Tessa Johnston</p></p><p><p>BIRT: RIN MH:IF789</p></p><p><p>DEAT: RIN MH:IF790</p></p><p><p>RET
2 CONC I: RIN MH:IF792</p></p><p><p>EVEN: RIN MH:IF793</p></p><p>OCCU: RIN MH:IF791</p>
