1 NOTE <p>[FT_Art_Na_MAacioch.FTW]</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Big Paddy Callaghan suggersts that the Poddidy nickname derivres from Patrick's father, who, he suggests, was also know as Poppidy. Dad recalls him l
2 CONC iving in the Ballure house up until the time of his death. A photograph existed of him in Ballure, suggesting a fairly tall man with lamb-chop whiskers.</p><p>He is noted in the 1901 Census, as being 
2 CONC able to read and write, and as being able to speak both English and Irish. His age in the 1911 Census is noted as 70, suggesting a d.o.b. of 1841. The 1911 Census also shows that he and Mary had 9 chi
2 CONC ldren in total of whom only Sally, Bridget and Maryanne survived. Dad confirmed that he knew that he had some uncles who had died young, but he was unaware that there had been so many.
