1 NOTE <p>[FT_Art_Na_MAacioch.FTW]</p><p><p></p></p><p>Also known as Mary Mc Grann, though the Grant name has survived in records. May have come from Croaghross/Portsalon, as the Grants appear to be from thi
2 CONC s area. D.o.b. is uncertain as she gives her age as 54 in the 1901 Census and as 71 in the 1911 Census. She had 9 children of whom only 3 survived. Two of the children who died were named as John and 
2 CONC Michael by Paddy Callaghan in the "Golden Virginia" document.
