1 NOTE <p>[FT_Art_Na_MAacioch.FTW]</p><p><p></p></p><p>Aunt Sally was held to be about 99 years old at the time of her death in the house at Ballure. She had never married, but had gone to the US, possibly a
2 CONC bout the turn of the century, with some of the Franks (her father's relations - possibly with her Aunt Sheila). She apparently returned and settled in Derry and ran a boarding house into the 1940s. So
2 CONC me of her nieces (Sally, Kathleen?) stayed with her. She moved back to Ballure possibly in the late 1940s or 1950s and lived with Grandma and Granda until her death. She was a slight wizened old lady,
2 CONC  with a fairly independent personality.
