1 NOTE According to Peter McCaughey he came from from Killeeshil Co Tyrone <p></p> <p>Mac Caughey, -Cahey    Mac Eachhaidh. Eachaidh is a personal name anglicized Aghy, cognate with Eochaigh, Oghy, once a po
2 CONC pular Christian name. Co. Tyrone</p> <p>MacLYSAGHT</p> <p></p> <p>Mac Caughan    Mac Eachìn.</p> <p>An Antrim and North Derry Name. Some families have changed it to MacCaughey.</p> <p>MacLYSAGHT</p> 
2 CONC <p></p> <p>(O) Mulcahy      Maolchathaigh.</p> <p>This name is derived from St. Cathach, not from cathach, warlike. It is numerous throughout Munster. In Co. Down Cahey, Caughey and MacCahy have been 
2 CONC used for Mulcahy</p> <p>MacLYSAGHT</p>
