1 NOTE <p>DF</p><p><p>Notes for ARTHUR (ART DONIE) FRIEL:</p></p><p><p>Art was at home for the 1901 Census, and was noted as an unmarrried farmers son who could read and write, and speak Irish and English. B
2 CONC y 1911 he had moved to a different location in Ballymichael, and had become married, but no details of his wife and family are on the 1911 Census. However, he is noted as a shopkeeper in 1911. The DOB
2 CONC  noted is from the IGI. Art is noted as starting at Ballymichael School on 24 November 1873 and left in 1888. He is noted as living in Rosnakill at that time and his father's profession is noted as sh
2 CONC opkeeper. This might substantiate the family recollection that Donie was evicted at some stage and went to live in Rosnakill (see separate note on this on Michael Seoirse's entry). Art was apparently 
2 CONC the first person to be buried in the cemetery at Fanavolty Church.</p><p>(Sept 2007) Note in a google search for Ballymichael came up with a reference to a Dept of Justice report (JUS8/48) on the burn
2 CONC ing of a hall at Ballymichael in 1934 - presumably at the time of the whole blueshirt thing.
