1 TITL Northern Ireland, Wills and Administrations
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT From the late 17th century until 1857 the Church of Ireland (then the State Church) was accountable for testamentary administration. An estate was administered based on if the deceased had made a will
2 CONC , the value of the property they owned, and whether their property was located in more than one diocese. The records in this collection originated from the following Church of Ireland Dioceses: Dioces
2 CONC e of Armagh, Diocese of Clogher, Diocese of Connor, Diocese of Derry, Diocese of Down, Diocese of Dromore and The Diocese of Kilmore. After this point, responsibility for the administration of probate
2 CONC  in Northern Ireland was transferred to the state. This collection contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government License v3.0.
1 _TYPE Collection
1 _MEDI 20237
1 RIN MH:S500238
0 @S500239@ SOUR
